The function is already a single 16-bit compare against a compile-time constant, so there is no algorithmic headroom; I keep the same semantics but express the comparison so the compiler emits a bare `cmp`/`setne` without any implicit widening or constant reload, and avoid an unneeded temporary.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL Field::IsValid(void) const
{
    return static_cast<FIT_BOOL>(profileIndex != static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(FIT_UINT16_INVALID));
}
```